WEBVTT

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:04.060
<i>Cursed tomes.</i>

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.230
<i>Books that house the author's 
emotions and memories,</i>

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.440
<i>and that emit a shining aura.</i>

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.870
<i>They are said to have various 
effects on their readers.</i>

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.900
<i>As a countermeasure against a string 
of cases involving these tomes,</i>

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.390
<i>a special national organization was 
formed to collect and preserve them:</i>

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:26.180
<i>the Imperial Library Intelligence Asset 
Management Bureau, also known as Fukurou.</i>

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.540
<i>In the 25th year of the Taisho Era,</i>

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.610
<i>Ozaki Hayato tells the girl about his past.</i>

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:38.550
<i>How he also lost his sister to a 
cursed tome with a flame-like aura,</i>

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:44.980
<i>and that those close to them also 
encountered cursed tomes in their pasts.</i>

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.710
<i>A string of tragedies caused by cursed tomes.</i>

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.880
<i>Loved ones are enveloped in flames.</i>

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:54.780
<i>What must the girl be thinking when 
faced with her inconsolable best friend?</i>

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.370
<i>This is the story of Kuze 
Tsugumi and her kidnapping.</i>

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.500
No!

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:35.670
Senpai! Senpai!

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.010
Senpai!

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:41.030
Hayato!

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.520
<b>Imperial Capital University Hospital</b>

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:52.520
Koruri-chan.

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:59.280
Thank goodness, Yoshikiri-senpai.
Thank goodness...

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:01.530
Yes, indeed.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.770
It is fortunate that he 
was rescued so quickly.

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.970
He'll need total bed rest, 
but can have visitors

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:10.060
for brief periods as soon as he awakens.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:16.280
Thank you so much for saving him, Ozaki-san.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.800
No, not at all.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.230
You too, Tsugumi-chan.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:26.280
Senpai was saved because 
you can see the auras.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.730
Yes, it truly is a relief.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.400
I'm going to stay here.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.270
I want to be able to see 
him when he wakes up.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.680
That sounds good.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:40.320
I'm sure he'll be happy to see 
you there when he wakes up.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.340
Thank you so very much!

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:48.830
Dance of the Evil Bird

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.830
-Karasu-

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.330
As you all know,

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:57.300
Yoshikiri-san was investigating the link 
between Karasu and the fake cursed tomes.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:00.710
The fact that he fell victim must mean...

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:05.090
It's highly likely that Karasu 
was involved in this incident.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.100
That is what we believe.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:14.060
Senpai was definitely getting close 
to finding out the truth about

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.610
the production of the 
artificial cursed tomes.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.860
Once I get confirmation, 
you'll be the first one I report to.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:25.610
Damn it. I'll definitely get 
some kind of proof next time.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:27.410
It must be Karasu.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:28.910
But...

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:33.120
The color of the aura was different.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.130
The aura's color?

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.130
The auras of the cursed 
tomes linked to Karasu,

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:42.840
while they might have 
been tinted blue or red,

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.180
have all been black in color, right?

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.640
Yes, that's true.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.140
But the aura yesterday looked just like

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:55.140
the one from when Hitaki 
tried to commit suicide.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.150
Yes, it almost looked like flames.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.670
I see.

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:06.660
Does that mean Karasu wasn't 
after Yoshikiri-san, then?

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:14.560
We'll have to ask Yoshikiri-san for more 
information when he's permitted visitors.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:15.660
Yes.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.860
It's a truly disturbing turn of events.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:19.850
Yes.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:21.170
Indeed it is.

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:25.790
Things seem to be escalating rather quickly.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.060
I came to bring you this.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:33.550
What is it?

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.060
Senpai's notebook.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:41.160
He woke up a bit ago and said 
he wanted me to give it to you.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:45.990
He said he put it together so 
information could still be passed on

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.510
if anything happened to him.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.060
Thank you.

00:05:51.670 --> 00:05:52.830
I'll read it aloud.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.940
"Inquiry results:

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:57.940
I believe the workshop where fake 
cursed tomes are being created

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.330
is in the basement of Nachtigal."

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:08.380
"They are made using a particular 
drug that influences the mind."

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:15.850
"Due to this, fake cursed tomes are 
being made by several authors

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:18.720
who are in an abnormal mental state.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:24.360
The one making the drugs is Professor 
Mozuyama of the Imperial Capital University."

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:30.680
We've always wondered how they were 
able to make the artificial cursed tomes.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.620
The use of drugs makes sense.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.120
I can't believe that's how they did it.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:40.590
Professor Mozuyama has been researching 
the mental sciences for a long time.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.510
"At the center of these authors 
is Sasagoi Touichirou."

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:51.580
It can't be...

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.560
Sasagoi-san?

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.560
As I told you earlier, please keep 
what we discussed today a secret.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.620
Understood.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.840
I appreciate you sharing 
the information with us.

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.780
Just as with Kuze-san, they may target you,

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:12.070
Shougo-kun, as the prime minister's son.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:14.070
Please be extra cautious.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.270
I will.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:16.550
Please leave it to me.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:23.830
It's so hard to believe Sasagoi 
is involved in this way.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.960
You both studied how to 
write novels together

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:30.110
at Moristune Saichou-sensei's 
students, didn't you?

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:32.880
Yes, and there were many 
others like us, as well.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:36.290
Sasagoi has published 
several books in the past.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:42.690
But now he's been reduced to running 
an antique bookshop? That's rough.

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:46.860
It's not a job you can keep up 
solely out of love for it.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:53.180
Sasagoi-san complained every time 
we visited him on our patrols.

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:56.800
But I wouldn't have thought it was because 
he was writing cursed tomes for Karasu.

00:07:57.630 --> 00:08:00.400
Perhaps he just wanted to 
write a book that badly?

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.430
He'd grown discouraged by
writing normal books.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:05.130
I've read them.

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:09.630
I've read the novels he wrote.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.340
I'll get straight to the point.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:25.400
I want you to join me.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:29.270
I will protect you.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:31.650
<i>It's kind of scary.</i>

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:34.030
<i>So many things have been happening...</i>

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.530
<i>Why has it come to this?</i>

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:48.090
With the major Western powers all currently 
inclined toward expanding their armaments,

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:52.160
we are fully aware of the fact 
that many people are concerned

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:56.090
about our country intentionally
steering toward disarmament.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:01.730
However, once war does break 
out and blood is spilled,

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:04.100
it is our young people who 
will be losing their lives.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:08.110
Those loudly protesting on the grounds of "national crisis" or "national interest"

00:09:08.830 --> 00:09:12.110
are never the ones to set foot 
on the battlefield themselves!

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:20.120
Is it truly worth it to build a prosperous 
nation on the blood of our young people?!

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:43.550
It will be all right, Shougo-sama. 
It's going to be all right.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:45.890
I know.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:52.470
Fortunately, a policeman noticed what was 
happening and threw himself on the shooter,

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:55.030
so the bullet missed and the 
prime minister was unharmed.

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:56.610
Who was the shooter?

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:57.560
A soldier.

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.530
They tried to take him into 
custody, but he killed himself.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:04.060
Apparently he was a subordinate 
to Lieutenant General Owase.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:11.390
The police suspect that Lieutenant General 
Owase might be the mastermind behind this,

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:14.880
so they have him secured and
are currently questioning him.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.780
But in reality...

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:20.050
Maybe it's actually Karasu and 
Shiginuma who are behind his actions?

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:24.560
Yes, there's the recent series of deaths 
of politicians around the prime minister.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:29.060
It would be reasonable to assume that 
this was the final act of that plot.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:34.320
What will they have planned next, 
now that it has ended in failure?

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.830
I want you all to stay fully alert.

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:39.070
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.570
Don't worry.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:44.080
As you can see, I'm fine.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:49.090
But I'm honestly glad you came.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.220
Thank you, Shougo.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:53.340
Of course.

00:10:53.560 --> 00:10:59.340
We don't know what might happen next, 
so you also need to be very careful.

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.360
I will.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.970
<i>So many things have
happened, and so quickly.</i>

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.980
<b>Ohbayashi Bookstore</b>

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:19.990
<i>It feels like we've drifted from reality, lost in 
the daily routine of patrolling bookstores.</i>

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:28.120
<b>Sasagoi Bookstore</b>

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:41.090
Hey, guys!

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:45.760
Good work today.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.880
You too, Tsubameno-kun.

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:49.160
Still working?

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.050
No, I just finished.

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:52.860
Would you like to join us, then?

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:55.970
We were just on our way to Flamant
Rose for the first time in a while.

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:58.650
Oh, I would love to accompany you!

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:00.110
Great.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:10.160
A cursed tome! I see an aura!

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:10.910
What?!

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:14.120
That man. It's a real cursed tome, 
not one from Karasu!

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.730
Got it. Kuze, you wait 
inside Flamant Rose.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:19.140
Huh? But...

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:21.100
It would be dangerous 
for you to go with us.

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:22.670
Okay.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.690
Mind if I join you?

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.690
Long time no see, Tsugumi.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.450
R-Rui!

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.240
But why?

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.770
I saw you come in here by yourself,

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.830
and I really wanted to see you, so I came in.

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:57.330
Welcome, sir.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.000
Coffee, please.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.330
Right away.

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:09.690
It's all right. I'll always be on your side.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:10.850
I heard.

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:15.480
Shiginuma Takashi has his 
sights set on you, doesn't he?

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:21.220
You should be very careful. 
He's a horrible man.

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:26.110
The only one more dangerous 
is Mozuyama Shirou.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:31.120
He's definitely interested in your ability.

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:36.040
That man only thinks of humans 
as animals to be experimented on.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:37.370
He's evil, without a doubt.

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:39.630
Rui?

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.510
Anyway, just be careful.

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:47.880
Um, what about you? 
Are you still with Kagutsuchi?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:50.870
Kagutsuchi is finally going to make a move.

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:56.240
We'll go to Nachtigal to destroy the workshop 
where they make the fake cursed tomes,

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:57.890
then hand Mozuyama over to the police.

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:02.380
Well? Will you come to Kagutsuchi now...

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.400
to be where I am?

00:14:08.260 --> 00:14:10.160
No... No!

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.570
I figured you'd say that.

00:14:13.570 --> 00:14:15.660
I'm not good at giving up, I guess.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.170
Kuze-san!

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:24.920
Kuze-san, who is this?

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:27.840
It's all right. He's a friend.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:30.680
I think that's my cue to leave.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:32.250
Later.

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:33.660
O-Okay.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:34.530
Bye.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:36.180
Oh, yes.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:42.750
Did I do something rude?

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:45.560
Not at all. We were just chatting, anyway.

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:47.070
Where are Hayato and Hisui?

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:51.200
They safely secured the man from earlier 
and are escorting him to the station.

00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:55.950
Which is why I am here to accompany 
you back to the apartment.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:19.850
Kuze-san!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:35.240
Tsubameno-kun!

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:37.750
Please get out of here!

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:41.130
Tsubameno-kun!

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:42.500
Tsubameno-kun!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.180
Tsubameno-kun!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.900
Kuze-san... run away...

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:46.990
Tsubameno-kun!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.020
I am so sorry!

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:08.020
Even though I was with her, Kuze-san was...

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.620
Kuze-san was...

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:12.510
This wasn't your fault at all.

00:16:12.510 --> 00:16:15.080
She's right. If we'd been more...

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.280
Yes, it's our fault.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:21.220
Kuze...

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:24.790
Hayato!

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.570
I'm going to Nachtigal and getting her back.

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:30.480
Wait. We don't know for 
sure if she's even there.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:33.800
Even if she's not there, 
we can still find clues.

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.270
We can't just sit here and do nothing!

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:38.180
Yeah.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:42.900
Let me reiterate that our job is the 
collection and management of books.

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:46.190
And we need permission 
from above to take action.

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:47.690
But...

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:50.350
However, this is urgent.

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:52.820
You guys go ahead.

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:54.700
I'll go report to the higher-ups.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:56.700
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:07.710
Get on!

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:10.710
Um... Is that bike...

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:12.710
Just get on!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.230
You can ride with me.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.730
Then I gladly accept your offer.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:33.530
Now then, we should get going, too.

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:34.740
Tokimiya-san...

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.380
I've been prepared for 
this from the beginning.

00:17:37.940 --> 00:17:39.990
I'll assume full responsibility.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:06.020
<i>Auras? Why are there so many?</i>

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:14.760
Welcome to my auction room.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:24.290
I had planned on waiting for you 
to come to me of your own accord,

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:27.790
but the situation has changed quite a bit.

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.790
Aren't they a splendid sight?

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:35.800
That one is dark purple, 
and next to it is pale blue.

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:37.910
This one is white.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:41.180
You can see auras?

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:45.310
Yes, though not quite as
consistently as you can.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:49.810
Long ago, I gained this ability 
in exchange for my right eye.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:54.770
I became captivated by
this otherworldly beauty

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:57.840
and collected cursed tomes 
by any means necessary.

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:00.320
What you see here is merely 
a part of my collection.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.080
My collection shimmers 
with fascinating light,

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.620
so much so that you can 
barely keep your eyes open.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.390
Let them fly!

00:19:22.230 --> 00:19:25.360
Put it out! Hurry!

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.300
Let's go! It's time to follow our path!

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:30.750
Yeah!

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:56.120
Nothing compares to the 
splendor of an aura's light.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:20:03.010
Fools who cannot understand its value 
must never be allowed to control it.

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:07.530
Yes, they are foolish and vulgar insects.

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:12.520
Freedom? Equality? Fraternity?
Civil liberties? All foolishness.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:15.560
The masses do not have the 
power to think for themselves.

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:17.520
They are better off obeying us,

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:22.530
the chosen nobility!

00:20:22.530 --> 00:20:23.780
You can't...

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:31.790
Let's go!

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:38.850
Hold on tight!

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:40.300
Got it!

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:52.680
How can you be so self-serving?!

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:56.880
Yes, this country is trying 
to follow the wrong path,

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:59.690
so I will cause the next great war.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:05.020
This country will be destroyed so that 
we can return it to its former glory.

00:21:05.020 --> 00:21:06.700
What are you saying?

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:11.320
The assassination of the prime minister 
failed because of that useless fool, Owase,

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:13.500
but we have already made our next move.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.710
A move that will once again 
lead this country to destruction.

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.460
You've gone mad!

00:21:20.090 --> 00:21:22.960
You're an awfully noisy little bird. Listen...

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:26.150
I'm going to Europe.

00:21:26.150 --> 00:21:30.790
Kuze Tsugumi, you will be coming with me.

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:38.480
And I will have you bear 
a child to succeed me.

00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:22.360
<i>It's me, Ukai Shougo.</i>

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:36.470
Chapter 10:  "White-Walled Birdcage -Trauma-"

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:24.140
<i>I'm on my way there now.</i>

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:25.920
<i>I hope you're safe.</i>

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:28.120
<i>I will save you, no matter what.</i>

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:31.210
<i>Actually, there's something 
I failed to tell you.</i>

00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:35.390
<i>I was doing some cooking just now, 
and I'd like you to try it when you return.</i>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:38.100
<i>It's my special beef stew.</i>
